<figure class="admission" aria-labelledby="r23-admission-title">
  <figcaption id="r23-admission-title"><span>Figure 1</span> Eight requests, three places to wait</figcaption>
  <capacity-burst>
    <p class="model-note">Illustrative rounds · eight requests arrive together · one round completes each working request</p>
    <div class="lanes" data-live>
      <section><p class="panel-title">Before a connection</p><p>Application queue</p><div data-lane="waiting"></div></section>
      <section><p class="panel-title">Holding a connection</p><p data-working-label>Doing work</p><div data-lane="active"></div><p data-blocked-label>Waiting for a work slot</p><div data-lane="blocked"></div></section>
      <section><p class="panel-title">Finished</p><p>Completed</p><div data-lane="done"></div><p>Refused immediately</p><div data-lane="rejected"></div></section>
    </div>
    <p class="explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite"></p>
    <div class="controls">
      <label>Connections lent <select data-pool><option>2</option><option>4</option><option>8</option></select></label>
      <label>Application queue limit <select data-queue><option>0</option><option>4</option><option selected>8</option></select></label>
      <label>Work <select data-work><option value="2">Two independent workers</option><option value="1">One shared row</option></select></label>
      <div class="playback" role="group" aria-label="Figure 1 playback"><button data-play>Play</button><button data-back>Back</button><button data-next>Next</button><button data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step></span></div>
      <div data-hold aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
    </div>
  </capacity-burst>
  <p class="caption">R1–R8 are requests, not orders. The two-worker case assumes two equal units of useful work can run at once. The shared-row case assumes one can progress at once. Connections have no setup cost here, idle pool connections are omitted, and real CPU, I/O and lock scheduling are not simulated.</p>
  <details><summary>Read the schedule as text</summary><p>With two connections and queue limit eight, R1 and R2 work while R3–R8 wait outside the database. After each round two finish and the next two borrow connections: all eight finish after four rounds. With eight connections, all eight enter immediately; only two work and six wait inside. Completion still takes four rounds. With one shared row, only one progresses per round. With two connections and queue limit zero, six are refused at once and two finish.</p></details>
</figure>
<script>
  import { stepper } from '../../figures/stepper.mjs';
  import { burst } from './burst.mjs';
  class CapacityBurst extends HTMLElement {
    connectedCallback() {
      if (this.dataset.ready) return;
      this.dataset.ready = 'true';
      const pool = this.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-pool]')!;
      const queue = this.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-queue]')!;
      const work = this.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-work]')!;
      const states = () => burst(Number(pool.value), Number(queue.value), Number(work.value));
      const player = stepper(this, { steps: () => states().length, draw: (n:number) => {
        const s = states()[n];
        for (const key of ['waiting', 'active', 'blocked', 'done', 'rejected'] as const) {
          const lane = this.querySelector(`[data-lane="${key}"]`)!;
          lane.replaceChildren(...(s[key].length ? s[key].map((id:number) => { const chip = document.createElement('span'); chip.textContent = `R${id}`; return chip; }) : [document.createTextNode('—')]));
        }
        this.querySelector('[data-working-label]')!.textContent = work.value === '1' ? 'Changing the shared row' : 'Doing independent work';
        this.querySelector('[data-blocked-label]')!.textContent = work.value === '1' ? 'Waiting for that row' : 'Waiting for a work slot';
        this.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent = s.active.length ? `Round ${n + 1}: ${s.active.length} working, ${s.blocked.length} waiting inside the database and ${s.waiting.length} waiting for a connection. ${s.done.length} completed; ${s.rejected.length} refused.` : `Finished after ${n} rounds: ${s.done.length} completed and ${s.rejected.length} refused. The pool limit changed admission; the work limit decided progress.`;
      }});
      for (const select of [pool, queue, work]) select.addEventListener('change', () => { this.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-reset]')!.click(); player.render(); });
    }
  }
  if (!customElements.get('capacity-burst')) customElements.define('capacity-burst', CapacityBurst);
</script>
<style>
